his clothes and his hair.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I mean, that's...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Makes sense.
-It balances out.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.960
So they say Trump hopes to drop
10 to 15 pounds this year...

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.096 line:92%
while Melania hopes to drop 239.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Ho!

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:35.335 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ho! Hey! Ho!

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.337
-This surprised some people.
Trump's doctor says he got

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
a perfect score on the
Montreal Cognitive Assessment,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a test that examines
someone's mental clarity.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we got our hands
on Trump's answers,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that they may have
gotten a little --

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.917
They've gone a little easy
with him with the grading.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-I think, well,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.119
just take a look. I don't know.
The first question was,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
"what is similar about a grape
and an orange?"

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.225
Trump said, "they're both types
of soda."

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It's correct, but --

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:05.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.801 size:78% position:39%
He's right, I mean...
-Next, they asked,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.438
"what is 30 minus 7?" Trump
said, "my approval rating."

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And he --

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoa!
-This is...

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they said,
"draw a square."

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump drew a doodle
of Mike Pence.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.780
It was actually a good drawing.
-Oh, my.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A good drawing, though.
-Very good drawer.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.952
Next, they asked, "what is
the name of this animal?"

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump said "Mufasa."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not wrong.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.128 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.129 line:92%
-And finally, they asked,

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
"what's the name
of this animal?"

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.532
Trump said "boobasaurus."
Well, I mean you got one --

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.434 size:84% position:42%
one wrong. One wrong
out of the whole thing.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, that's not bad.
-Not bad.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is pretty big. Today,
Senator Jeff Flake gave

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
a big speech
on the Senate floor,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.676 line:92%
and he compared President Trump

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Russian dictator,
Joseph Stalin.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:56.349
Trump said, "why, because we
were both elected by Russians?"

00:01:56.349 --> 00:02:00.386 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
After he was accused of making
racist remarks in a meeting

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.725 size:88% position:44%
last week, Trump tweeted
that his approval rating

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:11.297 line:92%
among black voters has doubled.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That story again.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.234 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.869 line:92%
Two times zero is still zero.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:18.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
Just so you know.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.674 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Doubled. "Doubled."

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.844
This morning, Eric Trump went on
"Fox &amp; Friends" and passionately

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.647
defended his father, while at
home the President was like,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:32.886
"where do I know that guy from?
I like him. I like him a lot."

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:33.553 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.522
You guys see this?
Yesterday in Japan, someone sent

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:39.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
